2026-11-05  David Walther

	* remote.c, sshw.1: new.  `winless ssh` / `sshw`: one ssh ControlMaster connection per session, a unix socket forwarded back to a relay on the
	desktop (the bell), port forwards added with ssh -O forward when a host's server needs a window, a static winless uploaded to hosts without one.
	* server.c, client.c, util.c: per-server secret (registry file mode 0600; header, cookie or /?t=); forwarded ports accepted only with it.
	* main.c: installed as sshw too; --features.  Makefile.in: remote-stamp builds the static binary; install links sshw.
	* tests/test_remote.c: fake ssh and browser; bell, options, upload-once, cleanup.  tests/test_server.c: the secret.

2026-11-03  David Walther

	* client.c: launch the window with a dedicated --user-data-dir (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\winless\\profile, $WINLESS_PROFILE overrides):
	an already-running Edge ignored --start-fullscreen, leaving a normal window with a title bar.
	* Renamed winview to winless (command, sources, man page, tests, environment variables, cache directory).

	* main.c, client.c, server.c, json.c, util.c, winless.h: rewrite in C (from the Python script); poll() event loop,
	hand-written HTTP/1.1 + Server-Sent Events server, small JSON parser/writer.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.in, install-sh: autoconf build; make check, check-asan, install, uninstall, dist.
	* tests/*.c: C test suite (testlib + unit + server + CLI tests); replaces the pytest suite.
	* viewer.html: page up undoes page down exactly.
	* winless.1, README, INSTALL, NEWS: updated.

	* winless, viewer.html: initial version.
	* configure, Makefile.in: GNU-style build and install (./configure && make && make install).
	* winless.1: manual page.
	* tests/test_winless.py: pytest suite for the server, the event stream and the CLI.
